{
 "_doc": "Crew leveling (change crew-leveling, mockup 39; owner, 2026-11-12: \"ensigns provide no bonus but gain xp overtime, and can be traded for prestige so you can get more experienced crew, or just level up your crew member\", \"need crew skill tree\", \"skill tree, each level gets a skill point, the player can auto level officers or pick paths on the tree to go down and specialize\", \"I wish crew leveling was kind of like a pyramid tree or something where some nodes can cross over, and some nodes have 2 or more prereqs\"). After the Starfleet Command 3 manual's officers (printed page 36: officers gain experience over a campaign, their worth and skills rising, and are swapped for more experienced ones from a pool for prestige; three skills to a station), in our own words and numbers. levels: the highest level; an officer has one skill point for each level above the first, so a level 1 officer (an ensign) has none and brings nothing. ranks and rank_level: the rank names and the level each begins at. xp_next: experience to reach each next level from level 1, spent on the promotion. xp_battle: experience to every officer of the crew for a battle fought, times grade_x by the mission's grade. xp_turn: experience to every officer for each campaign turn served. xp_per_prestige: the rate between experience and prestige, both ways: an officer transferred out is worth worth_per_level for each level above the first plus their banked experience at this rate, and a promotion's shortfall may be paid in prestige at it. hire_per_level: what an officer costs to hire from the pool, in prestige, for each level above the first. pool_levels: the levels on offer at each station each turn. retrain: the prestige to take back every point an officer has placed. trees: for each station a pyramid of skills on five tiers (5, 4, 3, 2, 1 wide, the apex at tier 5), each taken with one point: a skill with no prerequisite is open from the start; any: open once one of these is learned (most skills, so a path crosses from one side to the other); all: open only once every one of these is learned (the centre keystone at tier 3 and the apex). fx: the abilities it changes, each the key its battle rule reads and the change per skill; text says the same in words. auto: the order an officer on auto level spends points in, up the centre to the apex; past it, the first open skill.",
